\item 
    Use Cramer's Rule to solve this system for \( z \).
    \begin{equation*}
      \begin{linsys}{4}
        2x  &+  &y  &+  &z  &=  &1 \\
        3x  &   &   &+  &z  &=  &4 \\
         x  &-  &y  &-  &z  &=  &2
      \end{linsys}
    \end{equation*}

A linear system is equivalent to a linear relationship among vectors. 
\begin{equation*}
  \begin{linsys}{2}
     x_1  &+  &2x_2  &=  &6  \\
    3x_1  &+  &x_2   &=  &8 
  \end{linsys}
% \end{equation*}
% \begin{equation*}
  \qquad\Longleftrightarrow\qquad
  x_1\cdot\colvec{1 \\ 3}+x_2\cdot\colvec{2 \\ 1}=\colvec{6 \\ 8}
\end{equation*}
%</CramersRuleExample0>
